## Codex CLI Sub-Agent Operation

> The following rules apply only when OpenAI Codex CLI is installed and authenticated.
> Simple tasks (single-file/few-line changes, config edits, doc updates) can be handled directly by Claude.

## Architecture

```
User → Claude Code (Commander: Design & Integration)
  ↓
  Bash(codex exec ...) → Codex CLI (Executor: Implementation & Review)
  ↓
  Claude Code (Verification & Integration & Commit)
```

## Command Patterns

Use `codex exec` with appropriate profiles:

| Purpose | Command |
|---------|---------|
| Read-only analysis | `codex exec --full-auto --sandbox read-only "<prompt>"` |
| Code review | `codex exec --full-auto -p review "<prompt>"` |
| Debug / Root-cause | `codex exec --full-auto -p debug "<prompt>"` |
| Implementation | `codex exec --full-auto -p implement "<prompt>"` |
| With filesystem access | `codex exec --full-auto "<prompt>"` |

## Delegation Criteria

### Delegate to Codex when:
- New code generation expected to be 20+ lines
- Changes spanning multiple files
- Code review (Codex is more thorough)
- Complex refactoring or architecture decisions
- Root cause analysis of bugs
- Security vulnerability scanning

### Claude handles directly:
- Single-file, few-line changes
- Config file edits (YAML, JSON, TOML, etc.)
- Documentation / README updates
- Git operations (commit, branch, merge)
- User communication / Q&A

## Delegation Rules

### 1. Make prompts self-contained

Each Codex call is stateless (no memory of previous calls).
Include all necessary information in every prompt:

```
CONTEXT: Relevant background and file contents
TASK: Specific action to perform
CONSTRAINTS: Rules, patterns, and conventions to follow
OUTPUT FORMAT: Output format (code only, diff format, with explanation, etc.)
```

### 2. Delegate reviews to Codex

Delegate code reviews to Codex. Claude makes the final judgment based on the review results.

### 3. Retry on errors

Include the original task + error details when retrying.

### 4. Never pass through raw output

Never show Codex output directly to the user. Always verify, integrate, and report.

## Security Notes

- Never include API keys or secrets in Codex prompts
- Always perform security reviews on Codex-generated code
- Use `--sandbox read-only` for analysis tasks that don't need file writes
